# The secure element only answers to the configuration it was formatted
# against, which is not always the one this handset shipped with - a chip
# provisioned as the other model needs that model's set instead.
# init.joan.rc binds by SKU at early-init; this binds whatever FelicaParts was
# told to use on top of it.
#
# The property name is the same on every device that ships this, so it says
# "model" rather than naming the vendor or how the sets happen to be spelled.
# Here a model is the SKU string init.joan.rc already uses, which makes the
# values joan_dcm_jp and joan_kddi_jp.
#
# Lives on system_ext because the property has to be writable by an app:
# /vendor and /odm scripts expand ${} through vendor_init, which cannot read a
# system property, and a vendor property cannot be set from an app at all.
# init parses this one itself, so it can read either.
#
# Fires when the persistent properties are loaded, which is still long before
# anything opens these files - a bind mount is invisible to a file descriptor
# somebody already holds. An empty value, and a value with no directory of its
# own, leave whatever init.joan.rc bound in place; init ignores ENOENT.
on property:persist.felica.model=*
    mount none /system/etc/felica_${persist.felica.model} /system/etc/felica bind
